  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe finish-wall check reads the cone radius at the stock top for ordinary axial drilling moves.\nA 6 mm, 120-degree spot at 1 mm depth now verifies and posts inside a 5 mm pilot.\nA spot that enlarges the finished hole still reports a gouge and blocks the post.\n\nThe check uses the existing `Cutter::judged` and cone atom geometry.\nIt keeps the nominal radius for model sections, tool poses, arcs, lateral moves and unsupported cutter shapes.\nThe solid and stock checks still judge the actual cutter.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe previous tangency check compared the hole wall with the nominal cylinder.\nAt this depth, that cylinder remains above the stock.\nThe cone reaches a radius of 1.732 mm inside the 2.5 mm pilot radius.\n\n## Tests\n\nBoth shallow pins failed on unchanged `upstream/main` at `3c761b5bb`.\nThe app pin reported `Gouge { at: 1 }`.\nThe sim pin reported `Gouge { at: 0 }`.\nAll 12 pins now pass.\n\nApp pins:\n\n- `shallow_spot_cone_inside_pilot_verifies_and_posts`\n- `spot_cone_that_enlarges_pilot_still_blocks_post`\n\nSim integration pins:\n\n- `shallow_axial_cone_uses_its_radius_at_stock_top`\n- `a_cone_wider_than_the_bore_still_gouges_before_and_after_full_radius`\n- `untrusted_or_missing_cone_geometry_keeps_the_nominal_radius`\n- `a_declared_drill_rim_and_boundary_context_are_required`\n- `lateral_and_arc_feeds_keep_the_nominal_radius`\n- `explicit_or_modal_tool_axes_keep_the_nominal_radius`\n- `nonfinite_stock_top_never_clears_the_nominal_radius`\n\nHelper unit pins:\n\n- `verify::section::radius::tests::model_sections_keep_the_nominal_radius`\n- `verify::section::radius::tests::a_short_flute_cone_keeps_the_nominal_radius_at_the_shank`\n- `verify::section::radius::tests::nonfinite_stock_top_keeps_the_nominal_radius`\n\nThe old section source was copied from `git show upstream/main:crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs`.\nBoth shallow pins failed with that source.\nBoth complete pin binaries passed after restoration.\n\nEach disabled guard failed its pin by assertion.\nEach restored guard passed its pin:\n\n- Supplied model: red / green.\n- Boundary mode: red / green.\n- Declared drill rims: red / green.\n- Explicit and modal tool axes: red / green.\n- Matching cutter geometry: red / green.\n- Cone profile: red / green.\n- Arc moves: red / green.\n- Stationary XY: red / green.\n- Deepest endpoint: red / green.\n- Finite depth: red / green.\n- Cone top and shank: red / green.\n\nThe previous `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 15 steps.\nThe previous `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe checks cover the committed Rust files without further changes.\n`git diff --check upstream/main` passed.\n\nReview validation ran on head `0ee89fb64d9b92431c92731534beb5e234d24fad`.\nThe base was `upstream/main` at `35d65e03be24407e9701cb6bafa5dedf79c6d72c`.\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` ran the reached app and motion lanes.\nThe run completed 234 steps in 43.2 minutes.\nThe ordinary heavy tests had 97 passes and one failure.\nThe result was red: one step failed unexpectedly, `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`.\nThe test was `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`.\nIt failed at `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:144`, before verification.\nThe assertion was `the bore's path as the fix plans it`.\nThe observed counts were `(3158, 3130, 1141)`.\nThe expected Linux counts were `(4726, 4698, 549)`.\n\nAll eight dedicated known-fail checks matched their expected failures:\n\n- #1950: three checks.\n- #2845: two checks.\n- #2849: three checks.\n\nThe heavy gate remains red, so the readiness requirement remains unmet.\nNo source changed during this validation.\nThe latest quick gate rerun passed all 15 steps in 1.6 minutes.\nAll 265 selected tests passed.\nThis rerun used `upstream/main` at `08697d3c422a2f6ade1f3e1fd9970b16ed3177eb`.\nThe latest clippy rerun passed in 42.24 seconds.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -j 6 -- -D warnings` exited with code 0.\nThe head remains `0ee89fb64d9b92431c92731534beb5e234d24fad`.\nThe original heavy results above apply to this same unchanged head.\nNo source changed. New pins and mutation checks do not apply to this validation-only finding.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe GUI, release gate and a physical machine were not exercised.\nThe original QA project was not replayed.\nThe app pins use an original synthetic blind bore through the command and post paths.\nTool poses and other cutter profiles keep the previous radius law.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2714 and PR #2836 change `section::judged` in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs`.\nThis fix changes `section::tangency` and adds its private radius helper.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high.\n\nChangelog: Shallow spot drills verify with their cone footprint, while spots that enlarge the finished hole remain blocked.\n\nFixes #3020\n",
